  2284	*which* three are load-bearing (revenue movement, churn, and one measure of customer-revenue
  2285	concentration or efficiency), while explicitly naming the other four as color a business can review
  2286	less often. That argument is this book's, not Barry's, and the prose must say so in those terms — the
  2287	single biggest risk this entry can name is a chapter that silently smooths "here are seven things one
  2288	founder tracks" into "a founder should only track three," dressed as if the case said it.
  2289	
  2290	**Primary documents and evidence class (§5).**
  2291	- `nb-metrics-2019` — nathanbarry.com, published 2019-01-14, dateModified 2019-02-27, consulted
  2292	  2026-08-06. First-party, but a founder's own account of his own company: §5's **weaker** class,
  2293	  attributed as such in the prose, on the same footing as `nb-convertkit-5k` and `nb-direct-sales`
  2294	  already registered at ch. 08. Not audited, not independently verified — the underlying numbers come
  2295	  from ConvertKit's own Baremetrics instance, which the post says is open to public view but which
  2296	  this book has not itself queried; the book is trusting Barry's transcription of his own dashboard,
  2297	  one layer removed from the dashboard itself.
  2298	- **Not pursued.** ConvertKit's live Baremetrics/Open Startups page (the dashboard the post describes)
  2299	  was not fetched independently — `openstartups.html` and `os_2019.html` are already in the shared
